    "narrative": "The Austin Waves are positioned for a high-ceiling outing today, headlined by **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.**, who carries our top score of 83.85 against Trevor Rogers. His elite xwOBA and the favorable park factor drive this projection, making him the cornerstone of our lineup. Following closely is **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** at 74.56, who benefits significantly from a soft matchup against Lucas Giolito; the 5.37 xERA of the opposing starter provides the perfect environment for **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** to exploit his platoon advantage. Similarly, **Sam Antonacci** is a strong play at 63.14, surging due to his elite xwOBA and a prime spot in the leadoff role, while **Nasim Nunez** (62.09) remains a high-value MI start because of the targetable matchup against Giolito.\n\nWhile our core is strong, we are managing significant risks against elite arms. **Kyle Tucker** (55.12) and **Andy Pages** (49.35) face a brutal test against Zack Wheeler; while wind-out conditions provide a modest boost, their overall efficiency scores are suppressed by Wheeler\u2019s elite skill profile. We opted to prioritize **Dominic Smith** (58.81) over our bench depth, as his platoon edge against Bailey Ober's successor in the rotation offers a better path to category production. The most difficult bench decision involved **Brayan Rocchio** (47.66); he fell just short of our threshold, as his bottom-of-the-order placement (9th) and the skill of opponent T. Samaniego created a lower efficiency floor than the rest of our starting infield. Monitor the status of **Gunnar Henderson**, whose raw talent is being bottlenecked by a difficult matchup against L. Macko, dragging his score down to 53.01 despite his status as our primary power threat.",
